{/*
  ── THE ONE VIEW TRIGGER, AND WHY IT IS INLINE RATHER THAN THE SHARED MODULE ──

  `243:3` gives M-P2 and M-P3 the same trigger: IntersectionObserver at 25% of
  the section in view, once. src/scripts/motion.ts already implements exactly
  that and the homepage imports it, so importing it here is the obvious and
  architecturally correct thing to do.

  IT COSTS THE PAYLOAD BUDGET, AND THAT BUDGET IS ZERO. Astro inlines a bundled
  <script> only while it resolves to one chunk with nothing shared. With one
  importer (the homepage) that holds and the build ships 0 JS files, which
  specs/architecture/PERFORMANCE-BUDGETS.md records as a measured competitive
  asset and a deliberate ratchet: "the moment a bundle is legitimately needed,
  the budget changes by an explicit decision recorded as an ADR, rather than by
  a dependency arriving unnoticed." Measured on a scratch build, adding these
  two pages as importers splits the module out and emits four files, 1.45 KB.
  Small, and still exactly the unnoticed arrival the budget exists to catch.

  THE REAL FIX IS THREE LINES IN layouts/Base.astro: call initMotion() there
  once, so every route shares ONE entry, Astro inlines it again, the file count
  returns to zero, the cursor light and the per-section thresholds come back,
  and this block and its twin delete. src/layouts/** is outside this pass, so it
  is REPORTED rather than done, and what follows is the interim: the trigger and
  nothing else.

  NO try/catch AND NO FAILSAFE TIMER. Every call is feature-guarded so nothing
  here can throw, and there is nothing to rescue: the rest state of every
  animation on this page IS its final state. If this never runs, the page is the
  finished drawing.

  THIS COMMENT IS A JSX COMMENT AND IS COMPILED AWAY. A comment inside an
  is:inline script ships to every reader, and 2 KB of reasoning on a route
  already at 97 KB against a 100 KB budget is a real cost. The argument belongs
  in the source; the shipped script is four guards and an observer.
*/}
<script is:inline>
  /* The view trigger. See the note above this tag. */
  (function () {
    if (!window.matchMedia || window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) return;
    if (typeof IntersectionObserver !== 'function') return;
    var els = document.querySelectorAll('[data-lit]');
    if (!els.length) return;
    var io = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries, self) {
      for (var i = 0; i < entries.length; i++) {
        if (!entries[i].isIntersecting) continue;
        entries[i].target.setAttribute('data-lit', 'on');
        self.unobserve(entries[i].target);
      }
    }, { threshold: 0.25 });
    for (var j = 0; j < els.length; j++) io.observe(els[j]);
  })();
</script>

